# Developer documentation (`docs/content/5.dev/`)

The contributor documentation is one page per topic in
`docs/content/5.dev/`, listed below. Do not invent a parallel layout;
follow these pages.

**Always** read `docs/content/5.dev/06.architecture.md` before changing
layers, threads, blackboards, device drivers, network/HTTP, or where a
type belongs.

For UI colour, map overlays, dialogs, touch/hold, and in-flight safety,
read **User interface guidelines** in
`docs/content/5.dev/06.architecture.md`. That section adopts:

- NASA Colour Usage recommendations
- DOT/FAA/AR-03/67 (Electronic Flight Bags / EFB human factors)
- ICAO Annex 4 (aeronautical charts) and FAA HF design standards

Do not invent a parallel colour language. Reuse named colours in Look
code; keep high saturation and contrast for warnings and cautions.

User-facing behaviour also needs the **English user manual**
(`docs/content/1.manual/`), not only `NEWS.txt`. See
`.cursor/rules/user-manual.mdc`.

