## Writing these pages

The developer pages are part of the documentation site and follow the
same conventions as the other four sections; they are written once, in
`.cursor/rules/user-manual.mdc`. Read that rule before editing a page
here: it defines the frontmatter, the three names a page has (title,
navigation title, file name), the text conventions (80 columns, one
space between sentences, typographic apostrophe, when to use backticks,
italics, bold and quotation marks), the components (`::field-group`,
callouts, tables, figures) and how to check a change.

What is specific to `5.dev/`:

- The audience is people who build or hack on XCSoar, never pilots.
  Build, tooling, internal formats and processes belong here and go
  under `* development` in `NEWS.txt`.
- A page documents what the code does. When a page and the code
  disagree, the code wins; fix the page in the same patch.
- Data with a fixed shape (build targets, event names, attributes with
  one line of description) is a table. `::field-group` stays for
  description lists whose entries need a paragraph. A field group whose
  names are identifiers from the source (macros, XML attributes, file
  names) is written `::field-group{.name-code}`, which draws the names
  like inline code.
